a man in the west valley lucky to be  alive after police say his neighbor shot  him in the head it all happened a few  weeks ago at an apartment complex near  durango and sahara now austin culp is  sharing his story to try and help others  stay safe sasha loftus joins us with  this story you'll only see on eight  denise the man i spoke with tonight says  he's so grateful to be alive but this  entire situation has been really tough  he'd had trouble with his neighbor  before but didn't ever think things  would get violent like this  austin kulp is still recovering weeks  after he was shot in the head they said  there's still some bird shot and  concrete in my head it all happened  right outside his front door when he  says his neighbor who police have  identified as 49-year-old tyrone blanks  approached him with an ar-15 style  weapon turned around and went up the  stairs and then he shot the bullet  grazed his skull and left a hole in this  wall  blanks was later arrested after an  hours-long standoff with police i looked  down at my phone and all i see is that  my brother was shot in the back of the  head jordan milhoff austin's sister and  roommate says she was shocked when she  heard the news  they'd had run-ins with blanks before  but say they never expected things to  escalate this far even if it's not a big  deal it can turn into something like  this now as they try to get back on  their feet austin and jordan are forced  to face a mountain of medical bills and  say they're now being evicted from their  apartment it's hard i don't even have  insurance the situation that's  incredibly difficult to say the least  but no matter what austin says he's just  grateful to still be here thank god i'm  alive  now an arrest report shows blanks had a  prior felony conviction in new york he  now faces multiple charges including  attempted murder and possession of a gun  by a prohibited person if you'd like to  help austin and his sister we have a  link to their gofundme on our website
 

